# Hosting a network game with computer players of a mod (docs/MULTIPLAYER.md "The lobby"): the
# host form chooses who plays the computer empires (the fixture mod's Captain) and that they see
# everything; in the lobby each computer slot names its player and the host changes one (to
# Faulty), Add Computer brings another Captain, and the host switches "Computer players see
# everything" off again. Players who join see the same (computer-players-lobby.script).
# ci: fixture-data (it needs nothing but our own content: CI plays it on the test fixtures)
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --mods-dir=tests/fixtures/mods --mod=test.ai-fixture --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800 --seed=7 --open=multiplayer

wait-for item:"Host a Game"
click item:"Host a Game"
wait-for item:"Open Lobby"
# A free port of its own (the runner fills it in), and no router.
click item:"Port (TCP)"
key Ctrl+A
type "{free_port}"
key Enter
click item:"Forward the port on my router automatically (UPnP)"
click item:"Computer empires are played by"
click item:"Captain (AI fixture)"
click item:"Computer players see everything"
screenshot host-form.png
click item:"Open Lobby"
wait-for item:"Computer: Captain (AI fixture)"
assert-present item:"Computer players see everything"
screenshot host-lobby.png
# The second computer slot's player.
click item:"##slotplayer" nth=2
click item:"Faulty (AI fixture)"
wait-for item:"Computer: Faulty (AI fixture)"
click item:"Add Computer"
wait 3
click item:"Computer players see everything"
wait 3
screenshot host-lobby-changed.png
click item:Leave
wait-for item:"Host a Game"
